; ---- Apotheosis: DOM link extraction (extractLinks in WebCoreDriver.cpp).
; These MUST come from the DLL, not from WebCoreFull.lib. Document::links() builds a
; DocLinks HTMLCollection whose traversal reads the HTMLNames globals (aTag/areaTag) and
; caches itself in the document's node lists. Resolved from the static archive instead,
; the EXE gets a second copy of that code bound to its own never-initialized copies of
; those globals -> 0xC0000005 inside HTMLCollection::item(0). aTag above was already
; exported for exactly this reason; the functions consuming it have to follow.
?links@Document@WebCore@@QAA?AV?$Ref@VHTMLCollection@WebCore@@U?$RawPtrTraits@VHTMLCollection@WebCore@@@WTF@@U?$DefaultRefDerefTraits@VHTMLCollection@WebCore@@@4@@WTF@@XZ
?scripts@Document@WebCore@@QAA?AV?$Ref@VHTMLCollection@WebCore@@U?$RawPtrTraits@VHTMLCollection@WebCore@@@WTF@@U?$DefaultRefDerefTraits@VHTMLCollection@WebCore@@@4@@WTF@@XZ
?href@HTMLAnchorElement@WebCore@@QBA?AVURL@WTF@@XZ
?insertTextWithoutSendingTextEvent@Editor@WebCore@@QAA_NABVString@WTF@@_NPAVTextEvent@2@@Z
?s_defaultTimeoutInterval@ResourceRequestBase@WebCore@@0NA DATA
?hasPlatformStrategies@WebCore@@YA_NXZ
??_7ChromeClient@WebCore@@6B@ DATA

